     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "In a complete graph, each vertex is adjacent to every other vertex. The number of edges in a complete graph with <i>n</i> vertices is the sum of the whole numbers from 1 to <i>n</i> – 1. For instance, in an example in the lesson, a complete graph with 6 vertices had 15 edges."
